# ⚠ ASPIRATIONAL — this is the GATEWAY-variant env, for a topology that does not
# exist (no Caddy on the edge; edge and hbox are on different tailnets). The LIVE
# demo uses .env.funnel.example -> ~/.config/dregg/games-funnel.env.
# See deploy/games/RUNBOOK.md's banner and deploy/README.md.
#
# deploy/games/.env.example — the dregg games stack env template.
#
# Copy to hbox at ~/.config/dregg/games.env and fill the real values, then
# `chmod 600 ~/.config/dregg/games.env`. NEVER commit the filled file.
# Both units (dregg-web-games.service + dregg-games-bot.service) read this one
# file; each ignores the vars it does not use.
#
# ┌──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
# │ WEB GAMES SERVER (dregg-web-games.service — dreggnet-web-server)          │
# └──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘

# Bind address for the games web server — the TAILSCALE interface (hbox-dregg,
# 100.95.240.73), so the AWS gateway's Caddy reaches it over the tailnet. NEVER
# 0.0.0.0 (only tailnet peers may reach it; the public internet cannot). 8790 is
# FREE on hbox (8787/8781 already taken; OPS-RUNBOOK).
DREGGNET_WEB_BIND=100.95.240.73:8790

# Durable no-cheat Descent leaderboard (sqlite). Unset -> in-RAM (lost on restart).
# Re-verified by replay on boot. Lives in the units' ReadWritePaths.
DATABASE_URL=sqlite:/home/hbox/.local/state/dregg-games/leaderboard.db

# SHARED interaction-envelope audit dir (dreggnet-audit), read by BOTH the web
# server and the games Discord bot. Point every service at the SAME absolute dir
# (this stack + dregg-telegram-bot + the discord unit) so one `auditq correlate
# --dir <this>` joins a chain across them; per-process filenames
# (audit-DATE.<platform>-<pid>.NN.jsonl) keep the one dir contention-free. `off`
# disables the audit log entirely.
# ⚠ GATEWAY-VARIANT SANDBOX: dregg-web-games.service and dregg-games-bot.service
# run ProtectSystem=strict, so for a dir OUTSIDE their ReadWritePaths (this dir
# is under .local/state/dregg, not dregg-games) the audit writer would fail-safe
# to DISABLED. To use it there, add `ReadWritePaths=%h/.local/state/dregg` to
# those units and pre-create the dir. The live funnel/telegram/hbox-discord units
# carry no such sandbox and already set this via Environment=.
DREGG_AUDIT_DIR=/home/hbox/.local/state/dregg/audit

# ── SHIELDED OPERATIONS ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The deploy builds dreggnet-web with `public-shielded-games`; these variables
# decide which key-bearing operations are registered at runtime. Absence is a
# fail-closed disable, never a demo key fallback.

# fhEgg settlement upload authority. Set the comma-separated Ed25519 public-key
# roster and the minimum distinct valid signers together, or leave both unset.
# DREGG_FHEGG_QUORUM_PUBLIC_KEYS=
# DREGG_FHEGG_QUORUM_THRESHOLD=

# Proof-required Dark AMM v2. The protected regular owner-only file contains the
# canonical postcard BFV secret key; INITIAL_ROOT is the eight-comma-separated
# BabyBear state root emitted by the private-transition prover. Set BOTH. A key
# without a root would select legacy proofless v1 in the generic runtime; this
# public deploy script refuses that half-configuration.
# DREGG_DARK_AMM_SECRET_KEY_FILE=/home/hbox/.config/dregg/dark-amm-secret-key.postcard
# DREGG_DARK_AMM_INITIAL_ROOT=<eight comma-separated decimal lanes from private-init>
# Strict v3 also requires a relying-party-selected issuer roster. Each issuer
# sees the private transition and exact encryption seeds before signing; this
# authenticates same-opening but is not no-viewer custody. Set BOTH values.
# DREGG_DARK_AMM_AUTHORITY_PUBLIC_KEYS=<comma-separated 32-byte Ed25519 keys in hex>
# DREGG_DARK_AMM_AUTHORITY_THRESHOLD=<required signatures, 1..roster length>

# ┌──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
# │ DISCORD GAMES BOT (dregg-games-bot.service — dregg-discord-bot)           │
# └──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘

# REQUIRED — from the Discord developer portal. ⚠ ember places these; no prod
# token is ever committed or slung by an agent.
DISCORD_TOKEN=
DISCORD_APP_ID=
# 64 hex chars (32 bytes) — deterministic per-user cipherclerk derivation.
BOT_SECRET=

# The Descent daily-reveal announce channel (numeric Discord channel id). Unset ->
# the daily still rolls, it is only logged (no channel post). reveal_cron.rs.
DESCENT_ANNOUNCE_CHANNEL_ID=

# drand HTTP API base the daily-reveal cron fetches today's BLS-verified round
# from. Default (unset) = https://api.drand.sh (procgen_dregg::beacon::DRAND_API_BASE).
DRAND_API_BASE=https://api.drand.sh

# The bot's sqlite db (channels, gallery, characters). In the units' ReadWritePaths.
# NOTE: DATABASE_URL is shared with the web server above — if you want the bot and
# the web board in SEPARATE sqlite files, split games.env into two EnvironmentFiles
# (see deploy/games/RUNBOOK.md). One combined file is the low-friction default.

# ── OPTIONAL ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Explicit node URL. The games demo is node-FREE, so leave UNSET for the standalone
# public demo. Set only if you also want the bot's devnet-backed commands live
# against a testnet node (Phase 2).
# DEVNET_URL=https://devnet.dregg.fg-goose.online

# The bot's HTTP read surface (Starbridge RemoteRuntime / observability). Localhost
# only; not part of the games public demo. Defaults 0.0.0.0:8080 in code — pin to
# localhost here so it is never exposed.
HTTP_HOST=127.0.0.1
HTTP_PORT=8092

# ── POST-QUANTUM POSTURE (informational — set on the unit, not here) ─────────
# The games bot signs custodial game turns but is NOT part of dregg's proven TCB, so it runs
# the regular (unaudited) fips204/ml-kem crates. `DREGG_ALLOW_UNAUDITED_PQ=1` is set directly
# on the systemd unit (and the Dockerfile) — it is a required posture, not a secret — so you do
# NOT set it here. dregg-pq prints a loud "assurance VOID" warning at first turn-signing; that
# is expected for this bot. (The node installs the ~195 MB Lean-verified ML-DSA core; the bot
# deliberately does not.)

# ── NARRATOR (the AI dungeon master) ─────────────────────────────────────────
# Which hosted model narrates /dungeon and /descent. UNSET on the current deploy,
# so every room falls to the free tier (local Ollama if OLLAMA_URL is reachable,
# else the scene's own scripted prose). Absence is a fail-closed disable — there
# is no demo-key fallback and no uncapped spend.
#
#   chutes  — Bittensor inference via Chutes (OpenAI-compatible). Set ENDPOINT +
#             API_KEY + MODEL + the two PRICE vars (all four required).
#   chutes-tee — the SAME Chutes inference, but ATTESTED: the request is ML-KEM-768
#             encapsulated to an enclave key bound into a DCAP-verified Intel TDX
#             quote, and only that enclave can decrypt it. See the block below.
#   bedrock — AWS Bedrock (Nova/Claude); uses the standard AWS credential chain.
#   ollama / scripted / none — no hosted model (free tier only).
# DREGG_NARRATOR=chutes

# The OpenAI-compatible base URL (the chutes/openai path). Chutes serves TEE models.
# DREGG_NARRATOR_ENDPOINT=https://llm.chutes.ai/v1
# The Chutes API key (cpk_…). ⚠ ember places this; never committed. Empty = no auth
# (a local unauthenticated proxy only).
# DREGG_NARRATOR_API_KEY=
# The exact model id, from `GET https://llm.chutes.ai/v1/models`. No default on the
# openai path — it must be named. NOTE: naming a `-TEE` chute HERE gets you a model
# that happens to run in an enclave, with NOTHING verified by this bot — no quote is
# fetched or checked on this path. For real attestation use DREGG_NARRATOR=chutes-tee
# (the block below), which is the path that verifies before it encrypts.
# DREGG_NARRATOR_MODEL=

# REQUIRED for the chutes/openai path: the model's per-1k-token USD rate (the Chutes
# catalog lists per-Mtok; divide by 1000). Without BOTH, the model is UNPRICED and
# the metered layer refuses it — the run falls back to the free tier, never an
# uncapped spend. (On the bedrock path these override the default model's rate.)
# DREGG_NARRATOR_PRICE_INPUT_PER_1K=
# DREGG_NARRATOR_PRICE_OUTPUT_PER_1K=

# Per-run hard USD ceiling (reservation refused before the network if it would
# exceed this). Default 0.05. And the output-token ceiling per run (default 400).
# DREGG_NARRATOR_USD_PER_RUN=0.05
# DREGG_NARRATOR_MAX_TOKENS=400
# Sampling temperature (default 0.7). The receipt commits whatever text is produced,
# so determinism is not required here.
# DREGG_NARRATOR_TEMPERATURE=0.7

# ── ATTESTED NARRATOR (DREGG_NARRATOR=chutes-tee) ────────────────────────────
# The same Chutes/Bittensor inference, run inside a DCAP-verified Intel TDX enclave.
# Per turn: the OpenAI request body is ML-KEM-768-encapsulated to an `e2e_pubkey`
# that was bound into a TDX quote we verified against the PINNED Chutes measurement
# registry, and the reply is decrypted with an ephemeral key only the bot process
# holds. What that buys is confidentiality + the CODE IDENTITY of the serving
# enclave. It is NOT a claim about the model weights or the sampled tokens.
#
# ⚠ FAIL-CLOSED, and that is the point. With DREGG_NARRATOR=chutes-tee, if the
# attested backend cannot be built (no key, no `-TEE` model id, no measurements, no
# collateral) or a quote fails verification, the bot yields NO narrator and paid runs
# drop to the FREE tier. It never falls back to the plain endpoint — not even when
# DREGG_NARRATOR_ENDPOINT and AWS credentials are both still sitting in this file.
# (Proved by `attested_narrator_never_falls_back_to_an_unattested_backend` in
# discord-bot/src/pay.rs.) A failed attestation mid-run is an error on that turn,
# with NO inference attempted.
#
# The model — a `-TEE` chute; the plain id is a DIFFERENT, unattested chute.
# DREGG_NARRATOR_MODEL=Qwen/Qwen3-32B-TEE
#
# The Chutes API key (cpk_…), first of these that is set:
#   CHUTES_API_KEY  →  CHUTES_API_KEY_FILE  →  DREGG_NARRATOR_API_KEY  →
#   DREGG_NARRATOR_API_KEY_FILE  →  ~/.chutes-key   (files are read + trimmed)
# ⚠ ember places this; never committed.
# CHUTES_API_KEY=
# CHUTES_API_KEY_FILE=/etc/dregg/chutes-key
#
# MEASUREMENTS (what a quote is checked against). Prefer the local file: it is a PIN,
# reviewed and deployed by the operator. The URL form is fetched at construction and
# is only as good as that fetch.
# CHUTES_MEASUREMENTS_JSON=/etc/dregg/chutes-measurements.json
# CHUTES_MEASUREMENTS_URL=https://api.chutes.ai/servers/tee/measurements
#
# DCAP COLLATERAL (the Intel PCK/TCB material the quote is verified against). With no
# collateral there is nothing to verify a quote against, so the backend refuses.
# ⚠ The bot is built WITHOUT `dregg-chutes-e2ee/collateral-fetch`, so on this deploy
# CHUTES_COLLATERAL_JSON is REQUIRED and CHUTES_PCCS_URL does nothing. To fetch
# collateral live instead, build the bot with
# `--features dregg-chutes-e2ee/collateral-fetch` and set the PCCS base.
# CHUTES_COLLATERAL_JSON=/etc/dregg/chutes-collateral.json
# CHUTES_PCCS_URL=https://pccs.phala.network
#
# Accepted TCB statuses, comma-separated. Default (unset) = `UpToDate` ONLY. Setting
# it to an empty list is refused rather than silently accepting nothing. Widening this
# (e.g. SWHardeningNeeded) accepts enclaves on a stale/patched TCB — a deliberate
# operator decision, never a default.
# CHUTES_ACCEPTED_STATUSES=UpToDate
#
# How long ONE verification is reused before re-attesting (seconds; default 1800 =
# 30 min). A verification binds an instance's key for that instance's lifetime, so
# this is a staleness policy knob, not a protocol requirement. 0 = attest every turn
# (correct, and ~12.5s of cold path per turn). Invocation nonces are refreshed
# separately and do NOT trigger re-attestation.
# DREGG_NARRATOR_ATTESTATION_TTL_SECS=1800
#
# Endpoints (defaults are the Chutes production API; override only for a staging API).
# CHUTES_API_BASE=
# CHUTES_MODELS_BASE=
# HTTP timeout for discovery/attestation/invoke (seconds; default 120).
# DREGG_NARRATOR_HTTP_TIMEOUT_SECS=120
#
# ⚠ PRICING, honestly: nothing in the registry knows a `-TEE` model's rate, so it is
# UNPRICED and the metered layer REFUSES it (the run falls to the free tier) until you
# pin it. Chutes charges `-TEE` chutes per token like any other — no confidential
# compute premium — so set BOTH DREGG_NARRATOR_PRICE_INPUT_PER_1K and
# DREGG_NARRATOR_PRICE_OUTPUT_PER_1K above to the published rate for this model.
# HALF a price pins nothing.
#
# NOTE: on this path DREGG_NARRATOR_ENDPOINT is NOT used — the attested client does
# its own model→chute resolution, instance discovery and pinned invocation. Leaving
# the plain endpoint set is harmless; it is never reached.

# Free-tier local model endpoint (used when no hosted narrator is configured, or as
# the fallback when the budget is exhausted). Unset -> scripted prose only.
# OLLAMA_URL=http://127.0.0.1:11434

# ── $DREGG PAYMENTS (the per-user run-credit rail) ───────────────────────────
# The bot sells real-AI dungeon runs for $DREGG/USDC: a payment to a user's
# deposit address credits run-credits (1 credit = 1 paid /dungeon narration).
# EVERYTHING here is UNSET by default -> the rail runs DEVNET/MOCK (throwaway
# seed + mock watcher; no real funds). Going live is an operator env flip.
# Full go-live sequence + custody contract: docs/ops/PAYMENTS-GO-LIVE.md.
#
# ⚠ CUSTODY LAW: the deployed bot runs WATCH-ONLY and NEVER holds the HD seed.
# The seed lives ONLY in a SEPARATE operator "sweeper" service (DREGG_PAY_ROLE=
# sweeper) that derives per-user deposit addresses, publishes a public address
# book, and signs sweeps — run it in your secured signer, never on this bot host.
# ⚠ ember places every secret/real value below; none is ever committed.

# The go-live flip: devnet (default, safe/mock) or mainnet (real funds).
# DREGG_PAY_NETWORK=mainnet

# The WATCH-ONLY TRIGGER: absolute path to the address book the sweeper published
# (TSV of deposit-index -> base58 address). When SET, the bot constructs itself
# watch-only (holds no seed) and serves addresses from this file; a user not yet
# in the book is fail-closed ("being provisioned — retry"). When UNSET, the bot
# uses the seed-bearing operator config if DREGG_PAY_SEED is present (custodial),
# else the devnet/mock fallback. Set this on the public bot host to stay seedless.
# DREGG_PAY_ADDRESS_BOOK=/home/hbox/.local/state/dregg/pay/address-book.tsv

# The $DREGG + USDC SPL mints and the treasury sweep address (base58). Canonical
# mainnet values are in docs/ops/PAYMENTS-GO-LIVE.md — paste them here at go-live;
# they are NOT baked into committed source.
# DREGG_PAY_MINT=<the $DREGG SPL mint (base58)>
# DREGG_PAY_USDC_MINT=<the USDC SPL mint (base58)>
# DREGG_PAY_TREASURY=<the treasury address deposits sweep to (base58)>

# The Solana RPC endpoint the watch-only bot polls. A MAINNET config with no real
# RPC (or the devnet default) fails LOUD at boot — never a mock on a live network.
# DREGG_PAY_RPC=https://api.mainnet-beta.solana.com

# Pricing: atomic $DREGG per run credit (a payment of N credits N/this runs), and
# the USD price of one run (default 0.10). $DREGG runs get DREGG_DISCOUNT_BPS off.
# DREGG_PAY_PRICE_PER_RUN=1000000
# DREGG_PAY_PRICE_USD=0.10
# DREGG_PAY_DREGG_DISCOUNT_BPS=2000
# DREGG_PAY_OTC_DISCOUNT_BPS=1000
# DREGG_PAY_DREGG_DECIMALS=6
# DREGG_PAY_USDC_DECIMALS=6

# BACKGROUND PAYMENT POLL: how often (seconds) the bot re-polls every known deposit
# address and credits landed payments without a manual /credits. Default 60; 0
# disables (crediting then happens only when a user runs /credits or /buy-credits).
# DREGG_PAY_POLL_SECS=60

# Custody role. Default (unset) = watch-only (SAFE — never loads the seed). The
# SEPARATE sweeper service sets DREGG_PAY_ROLE=sweeper AND DREGG_PAY_SEED; the bot
# host sets NEITHER. Setting the seed here makes the bot custodial (higher risk) —
# only for a deliberate self-contained demo; the watch-only path is the default.
# DREGG_PAY_ROLE=sweeper
# ⚠ SWEEPER-ONLY, NEVER on the bot host: the HD custody seed (hex:… / 0x… / base58).
# DREGG_PAY_SEED=

# Explicit mock watcher on a NON-mainnet config (refused on mainnet). Rarely needed.
# DREGG_PAY_MOCK=1

# OPTIONAL — declare extra cross-chain treasury positions for the non-custodial
# /treasury view (base58 32-byte addr + asset; skipped if unparseable). Solana is
# always declared from DREGG_PAY_TREASURY + DREGG_PAY_MINT.
# DREGG_TREASURY_BASE_ADDR=   DREGG_TREASURY_BASE_ASSET=
# DREGG_TREASURY_COSMOS_CHAIN=cosmoshub-4  DREGG_TREASURY_COSMOS_ADDR=  DREGG_TREASURY_COSMOS_ASSET=

# ── GATEWAY / DEPLOY ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# These are read by the AWS GATEWAY's Caddy (deploy/games/caddy/Caddyfile.games
# runs on the gateway, NOT on hbox — set them in the gateway Caddy's environment,
# e.g. its systemd Environment=). They are NOT used by the hbox units.
# The public games domain the gateway's Caddy serves with Let's Encrypt TLS.
DREGG_GAMES_DOMAIN=games.dregg.fg-goose.online
# The Tailscale upstream the gateway reverse-proxies to (hbox-dregg:8790).
DREGG_GAMES_UPSTREAM=100.95.240.73:8790
